DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin((ln(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^(((x)^2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-6, 1, 4} U {-6, -4, 2, 6, 7} U {-6, -4, 2, 6, 7}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(({-6, 1, 4} U (-infinity, 13)) - {-6, -4, 2, 6, 7})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-9, -8, 4, 5} U {-8, 0, 6} U {-8, 0, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -8, 4, 5}) U {-8, 0, 6} U {-9, -8, 4, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, 0, 6})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, 0, 6} U ({-8, 0, 6} U {-9, -8, 4, 5} U {-9, -8, 4, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-8, 0, 6} U ({-9, -8, 4, 5}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-9, -8, 4, 5})) U {-9, -8, 4, 5}))) U {-8, 0, 6}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-9, -8, 4, 5} U {-9, -8, 4, 5} U {-9, -8, 4, 5}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`9+12-16-14/19`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('4.26315789474'),width=>1}
---

[`14*12+16*6`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>264,width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, 0, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -8, 4, 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A \cup A \cap B \cup A \cup B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup (A \cup B \cup B \cap ((A \cup (B) \cap B) \cup B)) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, 1, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, -4, 2, 6, 7\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x < 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`(A \cup C) - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, 0, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 8, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 8, 8>") x Compute("<-8, 0, 9>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 0, 9>") x Compute("<7, 8, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 8, 8>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, 8, 8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 8, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 8, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 1, -7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 10, -9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 1, -7>") x Compute("<-5, 10, -9>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 1, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, 1, -7>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 10, -9>") . Compute("<10, 1, -7>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
